    "created_at": "2022-09-09T06:42:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-09-09T06:42:43Z",
    "body": "I'm not quite sure I understand the observable consequences of the race. L2 is supposed to notify both workers and fulfill their promises, right? In the first race configuration:\r\n\r\n- the promise handler in w1 never runs, because the promise was never notified\r\n- the promise handler in w2 runs, because w2's promise was still in the queue\r\n\r\nIn the second race configuration:\r\n\r\n- the promise handler in w1 never runs, because w1 terminated before w1's promise handler got to run\r\n- the promise handler in w2 still runs, because w2's promise was still in the queue\r\n\r\nSo as far as I can tell they are the same. I must be missing something?",
